{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1381127-an-anarch-inner-circle","id":1381127,"title":"An Anarch inner circle?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-13T16:23:03-07:00","id":1381127,"title":"An Anarch inner circle?","content":"In V5 metaplot Anarchs have become a force capable of wrestling capital cities from the Camarilla's grasp. This seems to imply they have some sort of &quot;Inner Circle&quot; now. A group of Vampires who plan and strategize the moves of the movement, mobilize forces and twarts Camarilla counterattacks.<br /> <br /> If that's the case who do you think should be part of this &quot;Inner Circle&quot;?<br /> <br /> Here's a few names.<br /> <br /> <b>Robin Leeland</b>: survived to the current era while exisiting in England during the Dark Ages in open defiance against Mithras. Was one of the people who started the furores. Knows a lot about the Camarilla's movers and shakers.<br /> <br /> <b>Theo Bell</b>: Killed Hardestad and led most Brujah's away from the Ivory Tower and to the Anarchs. Keen tactical mind, superb fighter. Probbaly the most relevant Anarch leader in the whole of the USA.<br /> <br /> <b>Marcus Vitel</b>: The &quot;Emperor of Washington&quot; is a 5th generation Lasombra methuselah who declared for the anarchs out of sheer convenience. That doesn't change the fact his personal power and resources cannot be ignored.<br /> <br /> <b>Hesha Ruhadze</b>: Seems like he's keeping in contact with both the elders of his clan and those establishing themselves in America. Hesha has authority, other anarchs may dislike him and his clan but what he brings to the table is far to valuable to be dismissed...<br /> <br /> Anyone else you think makes sense for such gathering? At least a Gangrel should be there as well but I can't think of one who would fit...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T17:17:37-07:00","id":1381142,"title":"","content":"They have important members but are hardly on the scale of that. You might have Baronies working together like Jason Carl posits the Anarchs of LA doing, which fits your thought processes there. But hthe Anarch book makes it pretty clear that not everything is Baronies; you have as many Anarch ideologies as you have Kindred, even moreso now that the Camarilla pushes those they do not wish to associate with that direction. <br /> <br /> The Anarch book also talks about this with Bell, Hesha and Rudi as three particular pillars of the Anarch community, each representing a facet of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T18:26:21-07:00","id":1381164,"title":"","content":"I think the idea of any kind of monolithic organization among the Anarchs wouldn't fly. I think there are personalities who have a lot of influence, particularly the ones you mentioned (I'd also include Tyler, Salvador Garcia, Agata Starek, Rudi and, to a lesser extent, Anita Wainwright). The Camarilla is held together with structure and tradition, the Sabbat is held together by viniculum and faith, but the Anarchs are held together by force of personality and will.<br /> <br /> But that's how I roll. Your mileage may vary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T19:52:46-07:00","id":1381190,"title":"","content":"I think the Anarchs are best handled as an alliance rather than an organization with a clear coherent heirarchy. It's like the Allies with the fact that Marcus Vitel, Isaac Abrams/Jeremy MacNeil, the Council Chairman of Berlin, Rudi, and Party Chairman Yuri of the Brujah Council willingly aid one another against their shared enemy in the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Like FDR, Churchhill, Stalin, and De Gaulle, they don't necessarily LIKE each other and might even be fighting against one another were not for the fact they have a shared enemy in the Camarilla. However, for the time being they're all working together to undermine their foe as well as assist one another.<br /> <br /> Some are also far more powerful than others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}